en. Maybe just compute and output as float, JSON will serialize. We'll assume no rounding needed, or just use Python float.\n\nImplementation: iterate over calls, compute normalized_gain, check accepted condition. Build list of diagnostics dicts and accepted_call_ids. Return dict with keys \"accepted_call_ids\" and \"diagnostics\". Ensure no mutation of case.\n\nNow produce the JSON response with key \"implementation\" and value being the Python source as a JSON string. Need to escape newlines, backslashes, quotes.\n\nWrite Python source elegantly.\n\nEdge cases: division by zero? prediction_tokens is probably positive integer. If zero, need to handle? But spec says \"normalize gain by at least one prediction token\" implying tokens >0. We'll assume positive.\n\nReturn as per schema: accepted_call_ids array of strings, diagnostics array of objects with required keys.\n\nWill not use any imports beyond standard library.\n\nNow produce final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2141,"completion_tokens":623,"total_tokens":2764,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1792},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":434},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1792,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":349},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}